// Keleustes host management, v1 (docs/gaps/host-management.md).
//
// A belai host reports what is installed and configured on it (Host.Report)
// and runs host actions the console asks for: probes, config writes, product
// provisioning, upgrades and diagnostics. Every RPC requires the node's
// client certificate; the certificate's node id is the only identity used.
//
// Delivery: the node opens Host.Actions and receives every action addressed
// to it that it has not yet answered, then new ones live. An action stays
// replayable until the node files its first HostActionUpdate (the ack), so a
// reconnect re-sends it; the node de-duplicates by action id.
//
// Everything the server sends is remote, untrusted content on the node.
// HostAction.params are typed per kind and checked on the host; none of
// them ever reaches a model. Nothing in HostInventory or HostActionUpdate
// carries a secret value. Changes are additive only.

